      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "BCR-ABL inhibition converted chronic myeloid leukemia into a paradigm for molecularly targeted cancer treatment.",
        "attribution": "The proposed laureates capture drug discovery, clinical translation, and disease-focused validation within the stated contribution.",
        "maturity": "Long-term clinical experience and the broader influence on precision oncology make the achievement fully mature.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The discovery rests on prior foundational work on the Philadelphia chromosome and BCR-ABL biology not represented in this candidate."
