        "Ian H. Frazer",
        "Douglas R. Lowy",
        "John T. Schiller"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "HPV virus-like-particle vaccines created an effective means to prevent infection-associated cancers, a singular achievement in preventive medicine.",
        "attribution": "Frazer, Lowy, and Schiller provide a clear attribution for the vaccine concept and its critical experimental realization.",
        "maturity": "Widespread implementation and strong evidence for prevention of HPV infection and related disease establish long-term impact.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The ultimate population-level reduction in all HPV-related cancers depends on uneven vaccine uptake and long latency periods."
        ]
      }
    },
